      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chesterfield%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village’s name comes from Chesterfield in Derbyshire, England, the hometown of its early settlers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chesterfield%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A post office opened in 1838, and Chesterfield became an incorporated village in 1882.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chesterfield%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Chesterfield High School served the community from the late 1800s until its closure in 1947.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chesterfield%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
